Implement a complete TypeScript source file exporting:

```ts
export interface Track {
  id: string;
  title: string;
}

export interface PlaybackPanel {
  track: Track;
  source: string;
  placement: "bottom";
  height: 80;
  theme: "dark";
}

export function buildPlaybackPanel(
  activeTrackId: string | null,
  tracks: readonly Track[],
  sources: Readonly<Record<string, string>>
): PlaybackPanel | null;
```

Return `null` when `activeTrackId` is `null`, no matching track exists, the matching source is absent, or its value is empty. An empty active ID is malformed and must throw `TypeError`. Every track ID must be nonempty or the function must throw `TypeError`, even if that track is not active. If IDs are duplicated, select the first matching track. Return a new track object so later mutation of an input track cannot change the result. Do not mutate any input. A returned panel always has bottom placement, height 80, and dark theme.

Return only the complete source file; do not include Markdown fences or prose.

